// (3) out_xor: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether the corresponding input bit is different from its neighbour to the left. For example, out_xor[6] should indicate if c[6] is different from c[7]. For this part, treat the vector as wrapping around, so c[7]'s neighbour to the left is c[0].

module top_module (
	input [7:0] c,
	output [6:0] out_product,
	output [6:0] out_or,
	output [7:0] out_xor);

