Develop a module that performs various arithmetic and logical bit-shifting operations based on a clock input. The module generates outputs representing bitwise right and left shifts of specific 32-bit and 64-bit constants, which are controlled by an adjustable amount specified by the `amt` register. Additionally, it produces shifted outputs for specific positions, with manipulations on both unsigned and signed interpretations of the data. The outputs are aimed at examining different shift behaviors and demonstrating the effects of variable shift amounts on the 32-bit and 64-bit constants, making it useful for applications involving data manipulation and testing of shifting logic.
