Design a glitch filter circuit that stabilizes an input signal over a specified number of clock cycles to prevent transient voltage spikes or "glitches" from affecting the output. The module utilizes a timer to evaluate the input signal's stability against a defined threshold. If the input exceeds the threshold for a certain duration, it is considered stable; otherwise, if two consecutive low readings occur after a high reading, a glitch is detected. The output will hold either the stable input value or a predefined value when a glitch is detected, effectively filtering noise and enhancing signal integrity.
