Design a circuit that functions as a NAND gate. It takes two inputs, A and B, and produces an output Y that is the negation of the AND operation on the inputs A and B. The implementation involves inverting both inputs, feeding them into an OR gate, and then using a NAND gate with the output of the OR gate to generate the final output. The result is that Y will be LOW only when both A and B are HIGH, offering the characteristic behavior of a NAND gate.
