description:
Design a digital delay line that captures an input signal and delays it by a specified number of clock cycles, in this case, four cycles. The module uses a shift register to store the incoming data and outputs the value that was input four clock cycles earlier. The delayed data is produced on each positive edge of the clock, allowing for controlled timing in data processing applications.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input data,
  output delayed_data
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input data,
  output delayed_data
);parameter delay = 4; // number of clock cycles by which data should be delayed

reg [delay-1:0] shift_reg;
reg delayed_data_reg;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  shift_reg <= {shift_reg[delay-2:0], data};
  delayed_data_reg <= shift_reg[delay-1];
end

assign delayed_data = delayed_data_reg;

endmodule

